{ :reason :says "World W0 treats braking as a combination of reaction distance and friction-limited deceleration. On the four examples, it cleanly separates easy situations (CityDry, CityWet) from clearly risky ones (HighwayDryShortGap, CityIce). World W1 drops the reaction time and behaves like a bare braking-distance rule; W2 goes further by assuming good dry friction for everyone, so they both tend to be more optimistic and call some borderline scenarios safe. World W3 goes in the opposite direction: it amplifies W0’s stopping distance with a safety factor, which can turn marginally safe cases like CityWet into risky ones. In this way, the worlds illustrate how different simplifications and safety margins change the answer to the real-world question: 'Is there enough distance to brake in time?'" . }
  pe:rule 14;
  pe:uses
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W1 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W2 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W3 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :safeInWorld :W1 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :safeInWorld :W2 . },
    { :CityWet :safeInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityWet :safeInWorld :W1 . },
    { :CityWet :safeInWorld :W2 . },
    { :CityWet :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W1 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :CityIce :safeInWorld :W2 . }.

{ :check1 :ok true . }
  pe:rule 15;
  pe:uses
    { :CityIce :safeInWorld :W2 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W1 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W3 . }.

{ :check1 :msg "Check 1: on the icy CityIce scenario, world W2 is strictly more optimistic than W0, W1 and W3 because it assumes dry-road friction and still calls the situation safe while all others see risk." . }
  pe:rule 15;
  pe:uses
    { :CityIce :safeInWorld :W2 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W1 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W3 . }.

{ :check2 :ok true . }
  pe:rule 16;
  pe:uses
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W3 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :CityWet :safeInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityWet :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W3 . }.

{ :check2 :msg "Check 2: on these examples, the cautious world W3 is at least as conservative as the physics-based world W0: whenever W3 says safe, W0 also says safe, and W3 rejects all cases that W0 rejects, plus one more." . }
  pe:rule 16;
  pe:uses
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W3 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :CityWet :safeInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityWet :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W3 . }.

{ :check3 :ok true . }
  pe:rule 17;
  pe:uses
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W1 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W2 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W3 . }.

{ :check3 :msg "Check 3: all worlds agree that the CityDry scenario — moderate speed, dry asphalt, generous distance — is safe, so the models converge on an uncontroversial case." . }
  pe:rule 17;
  pe:uses
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W1 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W2 . },
    { :CityDry :safeInWorld :W3 . }.

{ :check4 :ok true . }
  pe:rule 18;
  pe:uses
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :safeInWorld :W1 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :safeInWorld :W2 . }.

{ :check4 :msg "Check 4: on the HighwayDryShortGap scenario, worlds W1 and W2 are more optimistic than the reference world W0 and the cautious world W3, since they classify the situation as safe despite W0 and W3 judging the available distance as insufficient." . }
  pe:rule 18;
  pe:uses
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :safeInWorld :W1 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :safeInWorld :W2 . }.

{ :check5 :ok true . }
  pe:rule 19;
  pe:uses
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W1 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W3 . }.

{ :check5 :msg "Check 5: for all scenarios that the physics-based world W0 marks as risky, at least one other world also flags risk; in this example set there is no case where only W0 detects a problem." . }
  pe:rule 19;
  pe:uses
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :HighwayDryShortGap :riskyInWorld :W3 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W0 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W1 . },
    { :CityIce :riskyInWorld :W3 . }.
